@rekram1-node I’m using OpenCode `1.18.31`, but I’m still experiencing the same issue during long-running sessions when using OpenCode through Zed’s ACP integration.

This is specifically happening with the Zed ACP setup:

<img width="1035" height="156" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/58d3a2af-d65d-417b-8c04-fb45406afec2" />

> Closing this because V2 now supports the requested behavior through [#41882](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/41882).
> 
> V2 keybinds use command IDs directly. The existing command can be bound in `~/.config/opencode/cli.json`:
> 
> {
>   "keybinds": {
>     "permission.mode": "super+shift+a"
>   }
> }
> 
> The original request targeted the V1 `dev` keybind architecture, so [#40334](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/40334) is now superseded.

I'm using **OpenCode CLI** _v2.0.10_ on **Windows Terminal**. But this `permission.mode` keybinding setting doesn't work. I've the below setting in cli.json. Anything wrong here?
```json
{
  "keybinds": {
    "permission.mode": "alt+shift+p"
  }
}
```
